# Reduced motion
@scenario tutorial_lesson_29
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: If you'd rather I stood still, that's fine. Let's play the same scene both ways and keep every choice within reach.
ginger: Change the motion setting in the topic menu, then replay Character movement or Camera movement.
> Compare reduced motion -> preview_still
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label preview_still
[if tutorial_still]
ginger: With reduced motion on, I stay where I am.
[else]
[move ginger rightmark ease_in_out_cubic 620]
[wait 620]
[move ginger rightmark thoughtful exprdur=90]
ginger: With motion on, I'll cross the stage and come back.
[move ginger guide ease_out_cubic 500]
[wait 500]
[move ginger guide normal exprdur=90]
[endif]
[jump check]
@label check
ginger: What must remain available in still mode?
> The same story and navigation. -> correct
> Only the title screen. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: Optional motion should never gate information or progress. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Optional motion should never gate information or progress.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_29]
[flag tutorial_done_29]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_6]
